1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,710
One man saved billions of lives and

2
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:02,736
helped kill millions,

3
00:00:02,736 --> 00:00:03,473
and both times,

4
00:00:03,473 --> 00:00:04,860
his secret weapon was the air.

5
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:06,010
It's 1909,

6
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:07,110
and the world is running out of

7
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:07,765
fertilizer.

8
00:00:07,765 --> 00:00:09,240
The best stuff is bird poop,

9
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:11,140
and it's so valuable that countries literally

10
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:12,032
go to war over it.

11
00:00:12,032 --> 00:00:12,807
The crazy part?

12
00:00:12,807 --> 00:00:14,645
Every breath you take is seventy-eight percent

13
00:00:14,645 --> 00:00:15,095
nitrogen,

14
00:00:15,095 --> 00:00:16,558
but plants can't crack it open.

15
00:00:16,558 --> 00:00:17,983
So a stubborn German chemist,

16
00:00:17,983 --> 00:00:18,658
Fritz Haber,

17
00:00:18,658 --> 00:00:20,533
squeezes air two hundred times harder than

18
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:20,983
normal,

19
00:00:20,983 --> 00:00:22,370
cooks it at five hundred degrees,

20
00:00:22,370 --> 00:00:24,133
and his little steel machine starts dripping

21
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:24,668
ammonia.

22
00:00:24,668 --> 00:00:25,131
Fertilizer,

23
00:00:25,131 --> 00:00:25,908
out of thin air.

24
00:00:25,908 --> 00:00:26,171
Today,

25
00:00:26,171 --> 00:00:27,571
that trick feeds about half the people

26
00:00:27,571 --> 00:00:28,067
on Earth.

27
00:00:28,067 --> 00:00:29,692
But the same nitrogen that grows wheat

28
00:00:29,692 --> 00:00:31,092
also makes explosives,

29
00:00:31,092 --> 00:00:32,542
and when the First World War cuts

30
00:00:32,542 --> 00:00:34,179
Germany off from imported nitrates,

31
00:00:34,179 --> 00:00:36,029
his process keeps its guns firing.

32
00:00:36,029 --> 00:00:37,029
Then he goes further.

33
00:00:37,029 --> 00:00:37,591
Near Ypres,

34
00:00:37,591 --> 00:00:39,679
he personally oversees a hundred and sixty-eight

35
00:00:39,679 --> 00:00:40,979
tons of chlorine gas,

36
00:00:40,979 --> 00:00:42,493
rolling into enemy trenches.

37
00:00:42,493 --> 00:00:43,056
Days later,

38
00:00:43,056 --> 00:00:43,893
his wife Clara,

39
00:00:43,893 --> 00:00:45,193
a brilliant chemist herself,

40
00:00:45,193 --> 00:00:46,243
takes her own life.

41
00:00:46,243 --> 00:00:46,993
The next morning,

42
00:00:46,993 --> 00:00:48,133
he leaves for the front.

43
00:00:48,133 --> 00:00:48,746
After the war,

44
00:00:48,746 --> 00:00:50,133
he's wanted as a war criminal,

45
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,521
so he grows a beard and hides

46
00:00:51,521 --> 00:00:52,342
in Switzerland.

47
00:00:52,342 --> 00:00:53,079
A few months later,

48
00:00:53,079 --> 00:00:54,386
he wins the Nobel Prize.

49
00:00:54,386 --> 00:00:54,699
Later,

50
00:00:54,699 --> 00:00:56,836
his institute's pest-killing research leads to a

51
00:00:56,836 --> 00:00:58,111
gas called Zyklon.

52
00:00:58,111 --> 00:01:00,011
A later version becomes the Nazis' gas

53
00:01:00,011 --> 00:01:00,749
chamber poison,

54
00:01:00,749 --> 00:01:02,111
and his own relatives die in the

55
00:01:02,111 --> 00:01:02,711
camps.

56
00:01:02,711 --> 00:01:02,923
So,

57
00:01:02,923 --> 00:01:03,936
by some estimates,

58
00:01:03,936 --> 00:01:05,336
half the nitrogen in your body was

59
00:01:05,336 --> 00:01:06,711
pulled from the air by the father

60
00:01:06,711 --> 00:01:08,286
of chemical warfare.
